  "question": "How well does AgentSSL perform on text classification tasks?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "AgentSSL demonstrates competitive performance on text classification tasks, particularly when programs are selected using oracle test performance. It achieves notable accuracy across various datasets and shot settings, as indicated in the results. For instance, in a comparison with strong SSL baselines, AgentSSL's performance is highlighted in Table 1 of the results section, showing its effectiveness in discovering programs that perform well in text classification tasks [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p6:para350:14].\n\nAdditionally, a specific comparison between AgentSL and AgentSSL across datasets and label settings shows that AgentSSL achieves accuracy rates such as 64.71%, 72.15%, and 76.93% under different conditions [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p25:para350:8]. Overall, these results indicate that AgentSSL is a strong contender in the realm of text classification.",
